[
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev02-01",
    "question": "<p>(a) Use the standard results for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r^{2}\"></span> to show that, for all positive integers n,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} \\left(r^{2}-r-8\\right)=\\frac{1}{3} n(n-a)(n+a)\"></div><p>where a is a positive integer to be determined.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(b) Hence, or otherwise, state the positive value of n that satisfies</p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} \\left(r^{2}-r-8\\right)=0\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>Given that</p><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=3}^{17} \\left(k r^{3}+r^{2}-r-8\\right)=6710\"></span> where k is a constant</p><p>(c) find the exact value of k.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>The constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-8\"></span> occurs once for each index, giving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-8n\"></span>. To sum from 3 to 17, remove exactly the terms at 1 and 2 from the sum through 17. Apply that same change of bounds separately to the polynomial and to the cubes multiplying <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>.</p>",
      "<p>(a) Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_j=\\sum_{r=1}^n r^j\"></span>. Expanding the summand gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_n=- 8 T_{0} - T_{1} + T_{2}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Substitute <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2=\\frac{n \\left(n + 1\\right) \\left(2 n + 1\\right)}{6}\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_1=\\frac{n \\left(n + 1\\right)}{2}\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_0=n\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Consequently <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_n=\\frac{n \\left(n + 1\\right) \\left(2 n + 1\\right)}{6} - \\frac{n \\left(n + 1\\right)}{2} - 8 n\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Simplifying and factorising gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_n=\\frac{n \\left(n - 5\\right) \\left(n + 5\\right)}{3}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=5\"></span>.</p>",
      "<p>(b) The roots are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0,\\pm5\"></span>, so the positive value is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(c) Use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_{17}-S_2=1510\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>The sum of cubes is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(17\\cdot18/2\\right)^2-\\left(2\\cdot3/2\\right)^2=23400\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"23400k+1510=6710\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Solving gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=\\frac{2}{9}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 9 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev02-01-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2018 · Q4, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
